`GET /api/social-rentals?limit=20&offset=0`

Auth: Bearer token + verified email

Response:
```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "total": 1,
  "items": []
}
```

BACKEND-ONLY WEBHOOKS

Do not call these from the React Native app. They are listed so web and mobile teams understand how server-side sync happens.

1. Airalo Webhook
`POST /api/airalo/webhook`

Caller: Airalo/provider backend.

Purpose:
- Receives eSIM events such as low-data notifications.
- Sends user email alerts when applicable.

2. Twilio SMS Webhook
`POST /api/twilio/sms`

Caller: Twilio.

Purpose:
- Receives inbound SMS/MMS.
- Stores messages in `virtual_number_messages`.
- Sends forwarding email/SMS when configured.

3. Twilio Voice Webhook
`POST /api/twilio/voice`

Caller: Twilio.

Purpose:
- Responds with TwiML to record voicemail for owned virtual numbers.

4. Twilio Recording Webhook
`POST /api/twilio/voice/recording`

Caller: Twilio.

Purpose:
- Stores voicemail metadata.
- Enables mobile playback through `/api/virtual-numbers/messages/{message}/recording`.

SERVICE MAP

Mobile-facing services:
- Laravel Sanctum: mobile token auth.
- Paystack: card payments for eSIM, wallet deposits, and Twilio virtual numbers.
- Airalo/eSIM provider: eSIM catalog, bundles, fulfillment, QR/install details.
- WalletService: USD wallet ledger, deposits, wallet purchases, refunds.
- Twilio: virtual number catalog, provisioning, SMS/MMS inbox, outbound messages, voicemail, forwarding.
- SMSPVA activation: one-time social numbers and OTP polling.
- SMSPVA rental: monthly social number rentals and rental SMS.
- Mail provider: verification emails, password reset emails, fulfillment notifications, forwarding notifications.

Excluded from mobile integration:
- Crypto payment endpoints and crypto provider flows.
- Web Blade page routes such as `/checkout`, `/dashboard`, `/assets/{type}/{id}`.
- Admin and debug routes.

REACT NATIVE SCREEN-TO-ENDPOINT MAP

Auth stack:
- Register screen: `POST /api/auth/register`
- Login screen: `POST /api/auth/login`
- Forgot password screen: `POST /api/auth/forgot-password`
- Email verification screen: `POST /api/auth/resend-verification`, refresh with `GET /api/auth/me`
- App bootstrap: `GET /api/auth/me`
- Logout action: `POST /api/auth/logout`
- Delete account: `DELETE /api/auth/delete-account` (Profile screen → Delete account button)

Home/catalog:
- Home highlights: `GET /api/landing`
- Browse all: `GET /api/allassets?tab=countries|regions|virtual`
- eSIM detail: `GET /api/assets/{type}/{id}/bundles`

eSIM checkout:
- Card: `POST /api/paystack/initialize` -> Paystack SDK -> `POST /api/paystack/verify` -> optional `POST /api/paystack/status`
- Wallet: `POST /api/wallet/pay/esim`
- My eSIMs: `GET /api/my-esims`, `POST /api/my-esims/sync`

Wallet:
- Balance card: `GET /api/wallet/balance`
- Ledger: `GET /api/wallet/transactions`
- Deposit: `POST /api/wallet/deposit/paystack/initialize` -> Paystack SDK -> `POST /api/wallet/deposit/paystack/verify`

Virtual numbers:
- Countries: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/countries`
- Country product: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/country/{country}`
- Available numbers: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/available`
- Card purchase: `POST /api/virtual-numbers/paystack/initialize` -> Paystack SDK -> `POST /api/virtual-numbers/paystack/verify`
- Wallet purchase: `POST /api/wallet/pay/virtual-number`
- My numbers: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/my`
- Inbox: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/{subscription}/messages`
- Send: `POST /api/virtual-numbers/{subscription}/messages/send`
- Media: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/messages/{message}/media/{index}`
- Voicemail: `GET /api/virtual-numbers/messages/{message}/recording`
- Forwarding: `GET/POST /api/virtual-numbers/{subscription}/settings`
- Cancel: `POST /api/virtual-numbers/{subscription}/cancel`

Social one-time numbers:
- Apps: `GET /api/social-numbers/apps`
- Countries: `GET /api/social-numbers/countries`
- Price: `GET /api/social-numbers/prices`
- Buy: `POST /api/social-numbers/buy`
- Poll OTP: `GET /api/social-numbers/check/{id}`
- Finish: `POST /api/social-numbers/orders/{id}/finish`
- Cancel: `POST /api/social-numbers/orders/{id}/cancel`
- Ban: `POST /api/social-numbers/orders/{id}/ban`
- Try another: `POST /api/social-numbers/orders/{id}/try-another`
- History: `GET /api/social-numbers/orders`

Social monthly rentals:
- Apps: `GET /api/social-rentals/apps`
- Countries: `GET /api/social-rentals/countries`
- Quote: `GET /api/social-rentals/quote`
- Buy: `POST /api/social-rentals/buy`
- Activate: `POST /api/social-rentals/{rental}/activate`
- SMS: `GET /api/social-rentals/{rental}/sms`
- Cancel: `POST /api/social-rentals/{rental}/cancel`
- History: `GET /api/social-rentals`

MOBILE IMPLEMENTATION CHECKLIST

1. Configure `API_BASE_URL`.
2. Build one shared API client that adds JSON headers and Bearer token.
3. Store Sanctum token securely.
4. Add global handling for 401, 403, 422, 429, and 502.
5. On app launch, call `/api/auth/me`.
6. Gate verified-only screens when `user.email_verified === false`.
7. Integrate Paystack SDK/custom checkout with returned `access_code`.
8. Always call backend verify endpoints after Paystack success.
9. Poll eSIM pending fulfillment using `/api/paystack/status`.
10. Refresh wallet balance after wallet deposits and wallet purchases.
11. Refresh `/api/my-esims` after every eSIM purchase or sync.
12. Use authenticated fetch/blob handling for MMS media and voicemail audio.
13. For social one-time numbers, poll check endpoint until SMS, timeout, cancel, ban, or finish.
14. Do not call provider APIs directly from mobile. Keep provider credentials only on Laravel backend.

HOSTINGER DEPLOYMENT UPDATE CHECKLIST

After this latest mobile API implementation, update these files on the Hostinger server:

Required runtime files:
- `bootstrap/app.php`
- `routes/api.php`
- `routes/web.php`

Documentation/reference files:
- `api.docs`
- `docs/mobile_api.md`
- `routes/mobile_api_endpoints.txt`

After upload, run these commands from the Laravel project root if your server uses cached routes/config:

```bash
php artisan optimize:clear
php artisan route:cache
php artisan config:cache
```

Confirm these production settings:
- The domain document root points to Laravel `public`.
- `APP_URL` matches the live domain, for example `https://spacechipltd.com`.
- `APP_DEBUG=false`.
- Paystack, Twilio, Airalo/Glo eSIM, SMSPVA, database, mail, and exchange-rate environment variables are set.
- Twilio webhooks point to:
  - `https://spacechipltd.com/api/twilio/sms`
  - `https://spacechipltd.com/api/twilio/voice`
  - `https://spacechipltd.com/api/twilio/voice/recording`
- Airalo webhook, if enabled, points to:
  - `https://spacechipltd.com/api/airalo/webhook`
- The Laravel scheduler cron is active:
  - `* * * * * cd /path/to/spacechip && php artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1`

Post-deployment smoke tests:
- `GET https://spacechipltd.com/api/mobile/health`
- `GET https://spacechipltd.com/api/mobile/endpoints`
- `POST https://spacechipltd.com/api/auth/login`
- `GET https://spacechipltd.com/api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>`

Expected mobile base URL:
- `https://spacechipltd.com`

Expected API paths:
- `/api/auth/login`
- `/api/mobile/health`
- `/api/mobile/endpoints`
- `/api/wallet/balance`
